\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces  Comparison of vergence (V) and accommodation (A) sensing approaches. Camera refers to imaging hardware per eye, from one camera to bench-top optics. Illum.\ refers to whether infrared sources are freely placed, fixed in a commercial tracker, or bench-mounted. Method refers to the sensing principle. Learning refers to whether the target is predicted by a learned model, a physical eye model, or a fixed formula. Accuracy refers to the reported error of the quantity in parentheses (high: $<0.5^\circ $ gaze or $<0.25$\nonbreakingspace D). Colours rate entries within each column for a compact wearable V/A sensor (green better, red worse). }}{2}{table.caption.5}\protected@file@percent }
